# sentence_id = 17
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = For their women exchanged natural relations for what is contrary to nature, and likewise the men also, abandoning natural relations with women, were inflamed with lust for one another, men committing shameless acts with men and receiving in themselves the due penalty for their error.
# literal_translation = For their females exchanged the natural use into that which is contrary to nature; and likewise also the males, having abandoned the natural use of the female, were inflamed in their desire toward one another, males with males working out the shamelessness, and receiving back in themselves the recompense which was necessary of their error.
