# sentence_id = 35
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = But if you call yourself a Jew, and rely on the law, and boast in God, and know his will, and approve the things that excel, being instructed out of the law, and are persuaded that you yourself are a guide of the blind, a light of those in darkness, an instructor of the foolish, a teacher of infants, having in the law the embodiment of knowledge and of truth — you, then, who teach another, do you not teach yourself?
# literal_translation = If but you a Jew are named, and rest upon [the] law, and boast in God, and know the will [of him], and approve the things that differ (being instructed out of the law), and have been persuaded [that] yourself a guide are of [the] blind, a light of those in darkness, an instructor of [the] foolish, a teacher of infants, having the form of knowledge and of truth in the law — you then, the one teaching another, yourself do you not teach?
