# sentence_id = 102
# translation_lang = en
# prose_translation = And without weakening in faith, he considered his own body, already dead (since he was about a hundred years old), and the deadness of Sarah's womb; yet he did not waver in unbelief at God's promise, but was strengthened in faith, giving glory to God, and being fully convinced that what He had promised, He was also able to do.
# literal_translation = And not having weakened in the faith, he considered his own body, [already] having been deadened already, being about a hundred years old, and the deadening of the womb of Sarah; but with regard to the promise of God he did not waver in unbelief, but was strengthened in faith, having given glory to God, and having been fully convinced that what He has promised, He is able also to do.
